; The placer of a BBC program's dynamic regions (lathe/docs/bbc.md, "One image for every machine
; with sideways RAM"; configurations.md, "Regions placed at run time"): the environment's
; `placer rt_place`. `$start` calls place() with the linker's list of the places of the dynamic
; regions (lathe/host/lk_dyn.py has its form) after rt_bbc.start and before `$init`, so before
; anything uses a region.
;
; The work is the module's, one placer for every tool of the image (lathe/rt/bbc/module.asm,
; `place`): this puts the list's address at $A8/$A9, the MOS's workspace for * commands, and asks
; with OSBYTE 143 for the module's service call $4C with Y = 255, a text no error has. If no ROM
; claims the call (a program not started from a module image that has the placer) nothing
; happens, and every region stays where it is linked, which is always right.
module rt_place

pub asm func place(places: ^byte in ax)
  STA $A8
  STX $A9
  LDA #143
  LDX #$4C
  LDY #$FF
  JMP $FFF4                         ; OSBYTE
end
